{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 proof of the Formal Conjectures statement that not every 2-hyperperfect number has the form 3^m(3^(m+1) − 2) with 3^(m+1) − 2 prime. The witness is A. Violette's number N = 3^16 · 129140227 · 256572153302107 · 225205396855537107298933866373 (OEIS A007593). The three large factors are proved prime by Lucas (Pratt) certificates, with all modular powers computed by a verified square-and-multiply function in the kernel. The divisor sum follows from the multiplicativity of σ, and a finite check excludes the special form.",
